head('4. Formal statement, bridge, and audit scope')
p('The reused source packet formalizes R162.Tree with leaf, unary, binary, and ternary constructors. R162.size and R162.edges give disjoint preorder-indexed vertices and edges; treeGraph is the associated loopless SimpleGraph. R162.arm follows the recurrence in Section 2; nanostar k is ternary (arm (k-1)) (arm (k-1)) (arm (k-1)). Only k &gt;= 4 is quantified in the conjecture, so natural-number subtraction at zero is immaterial.')
p('R162.orbit A = {m : there exist a in A and j in N with (Nat.totient^[j]) a = m}. The adjacency of phiGraph A is u != v and (phi(u) = v or phi(v) = u). R162.Realizable t asserts existence of a Finset of positive natural numbers A and a graph isomorphism treeGraph t to phiGraph A. The exact proposition is:')
