p('The discovery and independent-review receipts report strict Lean 4.34.1 builds and explicit-module leanchecker checks, with an inventory of 335 local declarations. The only transitive axioms reported are propext, Classical.choice, and Quot.sound. No Lean, lake, leanchecker, or solver was run in this manuscript task; the fresh work here is independent Python arithmetic and graph verification plus archive validation.')
p('The reviewer initially held the packet under an all-local-metadata rule: four compiler-generated partial runtime helpers exist, named R162.edges._unsafe_rec, R162.size._unsafe_rec, R162.arm._unsafe_rec, and R162.instDecidableEqTree.decEq._unsafe_rec. The independent dependency walk reports 271 safe, non-partial local endpoint dependencies and reaches none of these helpers. The root ruling resolves this as a qualified pass, invoking the ASEP 368807 precedent for unreachable compiler helpers; it does not pretend the four flags are absent.')
