head('5. Controls, significance, and literature limits')
p('The fresh checker verifies the source\'s D_2 witness {3, 256, 376, 384, 564}: 16 vertices, 15 edges, centre 16, maximum label 564, layers 1, 3, 3, 3, 6. The earlier discovery independent-control file has maximum 334 for its own different stage-2 witness. These are compatible, not conflicting computations of the same input.')
p('As supporting data, the stage-3 generators are {'+numbers(r['D3']['generators'])+'}. Their orbit gives 40 vertices, 39 edges, centre 128, maximum label 63314, and layers 1, 3, 3, 3, 6, 6, 6, 12. This independently verified control is not needed for the refutation and is not a separate contribution. The source neither proves nor excludes stage 3.')
p('Not every tree is realizable. In K_(1,5), the vertex 1 would be a leaf and its neighbor would be 2: among positive integers other than 1 only 2 has totient 1. But phi(x) = 2 has exactly the solutions 3, 4, 6. To see exhaustion, every prime divisor p of x has p-1 dividing 2, so x = 2^a 3^b; the totient product then gives just those cases. Thus 2 has at most four neighbors, including 1, which excludes K_(1,5), as in [1, Theorem 5]. Large fibers at unspecified targets do not prescribe a compatible iterated tree rooted at 1.')
p('The significance is modest: routine inverse-totient backtracking found an explicit counterexample to a published nonexistence conjecture. No general realization method, minimality, uniqueness, higher-stage theorem, or lower bound on search difficulty is claimed. Theorem 11 gives a single D_2 labeling, not an algorithm for arbitrary stages. The source\'s caterpillar and alkane constructions do not directly label this branching pattern.')
p('The retained bounded literature review inspected the primary source, its published successor, the accessible chemical references, and the primary statements of cached totient-asymptotic and weighted-dilation/fiber manuscripts. The latter concern totient counts or large fibers, not the prescribed finite orbit geometry. Registry and title screens found no matching refutation in their stated scope; they do not clear all proof bodies, private work, or deleted history. No new network searches were made for this draft and no priority claim is made.')
p('Specific unread items remain: <i>A graph related to the Tau function</i>, DOI 10.1063/5.0315935, is known only through retained metadata/abstract evidence; its full text was inaccessible. Rashid et al. [4] was also unread after a retained access denial. Neither is treated as affirmative evidence of absence of prior work. The root ruling gives qualified passes on fidelity and modest significance, with zero credit pending root acceptance. Campaign context is 41/60 new accepted results beyond 39 previous results; this draft assigns no additional credit.','Small2')
